<h1 class="admin-h1 mb-6">Site Settings</h1>

<div class="admin-card p-6 max-w-md mb-6">
  <h2 class="font-semibold mb-4">Site Logo</h2>
  <img id="logo-preview" src="<%= logoUrl %>" alt="Current logo" class="h-20 mb-4 object-contain">
  <form id="logo-form" class="space-y-3">
    <input type="file" name="logo" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp,image/svg+xml" required
      class="w-full text-sm border border-slate-300 rounded-lg px-3 py-2">
    <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">
      Upload New Logo
    </button>
  </form>
</div>

<div class="admin-card p-6 max-w-md">
  <h2 class="font-semibold mb-1">Membership Fee</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 text-xs text-slate-500">Charged once, via GCash, when a new applicant registers. Chapter admins cannot view or change this.</p>
  <form id="membership-fee-form" class="space-y-3">
    <div class="relative">
      <span class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 left-3 flex items-center text-slate-500">&#8369;</span>
      <input
        id="membership-fee-input"
        name="feePhp"
        type="number"
        min="0"
        max="1000000"
        step="0.01"
        value="<%= (membershipFeeCentavos / 100).toFixed(2) %>"
        required
        class="form-input pl-8">
    </div>
    <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">
      Save Fee
    </button>
  </form>
</div>

<div class="admin-card p-6 max-w-md mt-6">
  <h2 class="font-semibold mb-1">Payment Processing Surcharge</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 text-xs text-slate-500">
    PayMongo deducts this percentage from every GCash charge before crediting JPSME. Set here so the payer
    covers it instead of JPSME absorbing it — charged as its own itemized line on PayMongo's checkout page.
    Current PayMongo GCash rate (incl. 12% VAT) is about 2.50% — check paymongo.com/pricing if this ever needs updating.
    This is an upfront estimate; the admin Payments report separately shows PayMongo's actual deducted fee once each payment settles.
  </p>
  <form id="gateway-surcharge-form" class="space-y-3">
    <div class="relative">
      <input
        id="gateway-surcharge-input"
        name="percent"
        type="number"
        min="0"
        max="100"
        step="0.0001"
        value="<%= gatewaySurchargePercent %>"
        required
        class="form-input pr-8">
      <span class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 right-3 flex items-center text-slate-500">%</span>
    </div>
    <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">
      Save Surcharge
    </button>
  </form>
</div>

<div id="membership-required-module" class="admin-card p-6 max-w-md mt-6">
  <h2 class="font-semibold mb-1">Membership payment</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 text-xs text-slate-500">
    When optional, anyone can register and use the site straight away and may settle the
    fee later &mdash; their account and details are kept either way. When required, a new
    member is held on the payment page until their payment clears. Admin approval is
    unaffected by this setting.
  </p>
  <label class="flex items-center gap-3 cursor-pointer">
    <input id="membership-required-checkbox" type="checkbox" <%= membershipPaymentRequired ? 'checked' : '' %> class="h-5 w-5 rounded border-slate-300">
    <span id="membership-required-label" class="text-sm font-medium <%= membershipPaymentRequired ? 'text-amber-700' : 'text-green-700' %>">
      <%= membershipPaymentRequired ? 'Payment required to use the site' : 'Membership payment is optional' %>
    </span>
  </label>
</div>

<div id="payments-enabled-module" class="admin-card p-6 max-w-md mt-6" data-enabled="<%= paymentsEnabled ? '1' : '0' %>">
  <h2 class="font-semibold mb-1">Payments</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 text-xs text-slate-500">Kill switch for new payment checkouts (membership and event fees). Disabling this does not affect payments already in progress — their webhook confirmation still works normally.</p>
  <label class="flex items-center gap-3 cursor-pointer">
    <input id="payments-enabled-checkbox" type="checkbox" <%= paymentsEnabled ? 'checked' : '' %> class="h-5 w-5 rounded border-slate-300">
    <span id="payments-enabled-label" class="text-sm font-medium <%= paymentsEnabled ? 'text-green-700' : 'text-red-700' %>">
      <%= paymentsEnabled ? 'Payments enabled' : 'Payments disabled' %>
    </span>
  </label>
</div>

<div id="data-transfer-module" class="admin-card p-6 max-w-2xl mt-6">
  <h2 class="font-semibold mb-1">Data export &amp; import</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 text-xs text-slate-500">
    Download everything as one Excel workbook &mdash; organizations, members, events,
    registrations, payments and invitations, one sheet each &mdash; for offline tracking.
    The Organizations and Members sheets can be edited and imported back.
  </p>

  <a href="/api/admin/data/export" class="btn-primary inline-block">Export to Excel</a>

  <div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-slate-200">
    <label class="form-label" for="import-file">Import a workbook</label>
    <input type="file" id="import-file" accept=".xlsx"
           class="form-input file:mr-3 file:rounded file:border-0 file:bg-slate-100 file:px-3 file:py-1.5 file:text-sm">
    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">
      Only the <strong>Organizations</strong> and <strong>Members</strong> sheets are read.
      Nothing is ever deleted, and member accounts are never created &mdash; people register
      themselves, so a member row only updates an account matched by email.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
      <button type="button" id="import-preview-btn" class="btn-secondary" disabled>Check what would change</button>
      <button type="button" id="import-apply-btn" class="btn-primary hidden">Apply import</button>
    </div>

    <div id="import-report" class="hidden mt-4 rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm max-h-72 overflow-y-auto"></div>
  </div>
</div>
